#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/14-iot_Bluetooth_voice_control_relay.rst:19
msgid "Bluetooth Voice-control Relay"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/14-iot_Bluetooth_voice_control_relay.rst:29
msgid "This project integrates an Android app, developed using MIT App Inventor, with an Arduino Uno board. The app offers a voice input feature. When the user's voice input contains the word \"on\", the app sends a \"1\" message via Bluetooth to the Arduino, instructing it to turn the relay on. Similarly, if the voice input contains the word \"off\", the app sends a \"0\" message, signaling the Arduino to turn the relay off. Once the Arduino receives these messages, it processes them and turns the relay on or off accordingly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/14-iot_Bluetooth_voice_control_relay.rst:31
msgid "The Android application will be constructed utilizing a complimentary web-based platform known as |link_appinventor|. The project presents an excellent opportunity to gain familiarity with the interfacing of an Arduino with a smartphone."
msgstr ""

