#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/14-iot_Bluetooth_voice_control_relay.rst:202
msgid "5. Code explanation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/14-iot_Bluetooth_voice_control_relay.rst:204
msgid "Set up Bluetooth module communication"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/14-iot_Bluetooth_voice_control_relay.rst:213
msgid "This section initializes the Bluetooth communication using the SoftwareSerial library. This library allows the Arduino to have an additional serial port. The Bluetooth module's \"TX\" pin is connected to the Arduino's pin 3 and the \"RX\" pin is connected to pin 4."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/14-iot_Bluetooth_voice_control_relay.rst:215
msgid "Define variables and relay control pin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/14-iot_Bluetooth_voice_control_relay.rst:223
msgid "Here, we declare variables to store individual characters received from Bluetooth (``character``) and the complete message (``message``). The ``relayPin`` is initialized to pin 8, which will be used to control the relay."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/14-iot_Bluetooth_voice_control_relay.rst:225
msgid "Initialize serial communication and set relay pin mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/14-iot_Bluetooth_voice_control_relay.rst:235
msgid "In the ``setup()`` function, we initialize the standard serial port and the Bluetooth serial port with a baud rate of 9600. We also set the ``relayPin`` as an output pin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/14-iot_Bluetooth_voice_control_relay.rst:237
msgid "Read Bluetooth messages and control the relay"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/14-iot_Bluetooth_voice_control_relay.rst:264
msgid "The ``loop()`` function continuously checks for incoming messages from Bluetooth. When a message is received, each character is appended to the ``message`` string. Once the ``#`` character is detected, the message is considered complete. We then remove the ``#``, print a debug message, and check the content. If it's \"1\", the relay is turned on; if \"0\", it's turned off. The ``message`` string is then cleared, and we wait briefly before checking for the next message."
msgstr ""
